text:
dani: Quick report - onboarding sampleapp is flaky when using embeddings + rerank across Node & Python SDKs. Two UX bugs compounding: Node helper sometimes double-nests single-item batches and rerank responses use inconsistent score keys (we've seen score, rankingScore, and confidence). Also noticed duplicate processing when auth middleware retries.

omar: ugh. any short repro?

dani: Yep, tiny repro below. Node helper behavior vs Python and sample rerank payloads: 

```js
// Node sampleapp helper output
const batch = batching.make([{text: 'query'}]);
// batch -> [ [0.001, 0.002, ...] ] // nested array for single input

// API returns: { data: [[...]] }
```

```py
# Python helper
b = batching.make(['query'])
# b -> [0.001, 0.002, ...] // flat vector
# API returns: { data: [...] }
```

// Rerank examples we've seen from hosted:
{ "results": [{ "id": "docA", "score": 0.81 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "docA", "rankingScore": 0.81 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "docA", "confidence": 0.81 }] }

// Auth retry issue: Node auth middleware refreshes token on 401 then resends request but drops x-rw-client-id header, server processes twice for side-effecting endpoints.

kelly: I can reproduce the Node nesting locally. Looks like the helper wraps outputs unconditionally; when consumers also wrap, you end up with shape [[vector]] vs expected [vector] or [[vector]] depending on contract. We should choose one explicit contract and enforce it.

lee: For rerank key variance - SDK should accept multiple keys and normalize to `score` in the public response. Fallback order I recommend: score > rankingScore > confidence. Add schema validation in CI so model rollouts that change field names fail the SDK test.

omar: Workaround I added to the sampleapp template so onboarding isn't blocked. Normalize embedding shape + normalize rerank keys client-side: 

```js
// normalize embedding response to list-of-list
let emb = resp.data;
if (!Array.isArray(emb[0])) emb = [emb];

// normalize rerank result
const mapped = res.results.map(r => ({
  id: r.id,
  score: r.score ?? r.rankingScore ?? r.confidence
}));
```

kelly: Nice. I'll open a small PR for the node batching helper to make its contract explicit: always return array-of-vectors (list-of-list) at the helper boundary and add unit tests for n=1 and n>1. Also will add a short docstring.

lee: I'll add the SDK mapping patch and a JSON schema for rerank responses in the SDK tests. Will also add a regression test that ensures normalized output shape and normalized scores.

ops-bot: Created ticket DEVEX-3001: "sampleapp DX: embed batching shape mismatch + rerank score key variance + auth retry idempotency". Linked PRs requested: prs/7122 (node-batching-clarify), prs/7123 (sdk-rerank-normalize), prs/7124 (auth-retry-preserve-id). Please add an e2e parity test in sampleapp that runs both Node & Python flows and asserts identical normalized outputs.

sdk-bot: CI suggestion: add a lightweight e2e that calls embeddings+rerank with a fixed fixture and asserts (1) embeddings normalized to shape [N][D], (2) rerank mapped to `score` present for each result, (3) no duplicate side-effects when auth triggers token refresh.

dani: Thanks — will land short-term workaround in sampleapp and wait for the three PRs. Also updating onboarding docs with a note about possible rerank key differences and that helpers return list-of-list. Will ping once PRs are linked to DEVEX-3001. :+1:
